{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfgEqpmjrqFYdbc1P7YPG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate, a model named `personal_engagement_lapse_tally_switch`, and it passes the self-check (prints `OK`). It hasn't been through the novelty, convergence or 30-minute fit-time checks yet.\n\n**Hypothesis:** each person has their own rate of not engaging with a trial and just guessing a side, drawn from a population distribution. When they do engage, they judge randomness the way the current best model, `rule_built_tally_switch_triplet`, says they do. The new claim is only this per-person guessing rate. It gives a direct answer to the critique's one discrepancy that survives the FDR (people differ more than the best model allows in how often they agree with the majority, q = 0.048).\n\n**Where it should disagree with the best model:** on pairs where nearly everyone agrees, such as a rule-built or streaky sequence against a balanced, irregular one. The best model predicts consistently extreme choice rates there. This model predicts that some people stay close to 50/50.\n\n**Implementation:** `candidate.py` is the best model's code plus the per-person guessing rate. The prior puts the typical guessing rate at about 8%. `p_left` mixes a 50/50 guess with the engaged choice and is clipped to stay strictly between 0 and 1.\n\n**Self-check results:**\n- **Fit:** the short smoke fit gave an ELPD-LOO of −3394.8, against −3413.6 for the best model's full fit. That comparison doesn't mean much, because a 100-draw, single-chain fit is very noisy.\n- **Unreliable LOO estimate:** 6.3% of trials had a high Pareto k, over the 1% tolerance. This may just be the short fit. If it holds up in the full fit, the model's ELPD won't be trusted, and it can't be the exported winner.\n- **Speed:** the check took 8m49s for this model and 6m15s for the best model, so it's about 40% slower. The best model was admitted, so this one should fit in time, but the 30-minute limit is a real risk if the full fit grows by the same factor.\n\nThe model also deviates from what the exploratory brief asks for. That brief forbids combining mechanisms from other hypotheses, but this model reuses the best model's whole judgement and adds only the guessing rate. It's closer to a refinement of the best model than a new mechanism, so it could be judged that way.\n\nOne cleanup was blocked: I copied the best model into `/tmp/inc_check` to time its check, and permission to delete that directory was denied. It is still there.\n\nFiles are in `experiment3/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_1/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":328,"cache_read_input_tokens":81142,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":328,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5839abd1-db92-4da7-a56c-c9bdb221259d","uuid":"68914038-0ec7-4392-bd94-776257e71a3e","timestamp":"2026-10-04T00:20:16.460Z","request_id":"req_011CfgEqpHE1DRcHex1xySMQ"}
